1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Every AI coding tool has the same problem. To help you, it reads your code -- and your code is full of secrets.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,000
SecretNAT is on by default -- it sits between rysh and the model. The provider only ever sees synthetic tokens.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Watch. I paste a live Stripe key and ask about it. The model answers correctly -- it knows it's a live key. But look closely: it's reasoning about a token, S-N-A-T zero-zero-zero-zero-zero-one, never your real value.

4
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Rysh kept a reversible map. Snat list shows every token it swapped in -- tokens only. And when you need the real value, snat get hands it back, right here on your machine. The model never sees it.

5
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Now the receipts. Step out of rysh, and grep every byte it sent the model. The real key? Zero. The model saw a look-alike rysh can reverse and the provider can't. That's NAT -- for secrets.

6
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
You can unmask it. The model can't.

